             limiter, health-state tracker, inbound rate-limit
             middleware, FileManagement runtime). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeRuntimeServices.fs" />
        <!-- Domain state stores (entity, result,
             lineage, conversation, config, module query bus,
             feature flags). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeStores.fs" />
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeObservability.fs" />
        <!-- Per-tenant team/invite/permission stores
             + post-bootstrap validators (TeamCreationPolicy,
             BootstrapTeam, PendingInviteStoreInstance,
             SurfaceCoherence) + BootstrapTeam runtime. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeTeamRuntime.fs" />
        <!-- Health checks + smoke tests + first-party
             CSP contributors. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeHealthSmoke.fs" />
        <!-- Per-request scope/subject/surface
             registration block (`IStorageScopeResolver`,
             `ISubjectResolver`, `SurfaceRequirementRegistry`,
             `IAnonymousSessionMigrator`, scoped `AccessContext`
             factory, `IHttpContextAccessor`, session). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeScopeResolver.fs" />
        <!-- Host abstraction returned by `compose`. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\IServerHost.fs" />
        <!-- Idempotent, mode-gated seed-pack application.
             Invoked from ComposeBootstrap.buildAndRunHost (below) after the
             DI container is built, so it compiles before ComposeBootstrap.fs. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\SeedDataLoader.fs" />
        <!-- Bootstrap finalisation (preflight + CSP
             aggregate) + Build branch returning `IServerHost`. Sits
             after `IServerHost.fs` because `buildAndRunHost` returns
             the interface defined there. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeBootstrap.fs" />
        <!-- Registers the four first-party ITenantLifecycle
             hooks + snapshot when TenantLifecycle = EnabledTenantLifecycle.
             After the hooks + handler it references; before SDK.Server
             (which calls registerTenantLifecycle). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\ComposeTenantLifecycle.fs" />
        <!-- Opt-in print-config / validate-config startup modes.
             After ComposeBootstrap (returns IServerHost) + ConfigKeyDescriptor
             registry; consumed by SDK.Server.compose's tail. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\StartupModes.fs" />
        <Compile Include="Server\SDK.Server.fs" />
        <!-- Introspectable composition manifest: generic
             read-only enumeration of the composed surface (modules,
             companion slots, datatypes, tools) by stable ComponentId.
             Types + element constructors only (depends on ComponentId);
             the ServerApp.compositionManifest projector lives in ServerApp
             (next), so this must compile before it. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionManifest.fs" />
        <!-- Composition structural diff: CompositionDelta +
             CompositionDiff.diff, an id-keyed / order-independent diff of two
             CompositionManifests (added / removed / changed modules, companion
             slots, datatypes, tools + config-knob value moves). Pure companion
             to the manifest — depends only on CompositionManifest +
             ComponentId. Feeds the golden-file CI gate. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDiff.fs" />
        <!-- Composition capability sandbox (runtime default-deny):
             ICompositionCapabilityGate enforces the effect-join at
             runtime — a component may only exercise capabilities at or below
             its declared CompanionCapability envelope (resolved from a
             CapabilitySignature keyed by ComponentId), default-deny anything
             beyond, every deny observable. Generalises the
             authorizer-gated Invoke to the whole composition (guardInvoke
             bridge). Opt-in — `disabled` passthrough is the byte-identical
             default (GP 11/13); depends only on Core CompanionCapability +
             the registry types. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionCapabilityGate.fs" />
        <!-- Boot verification preflight + the verified composition
             profile: derives nothing itself, but asks at startup whether the
             running CompositionManifest is the one the sealed deploy
             record covers (seal, artifact digests, binding-belongs-to-record,
             component-by-component agreement), and carries the opt-in profile
             under which that check is refuse-on-drift, the capability
             gate is mandatory, and ExecutionProfileGate is applied.
             After CompositionManifest + CompositionCapabilityGate (reads both),
             after DeployRecords (reuses its verification) and AuditLog (emits
             verdicts + refusals through the audit seam); before ServerApp,
             which appends the one-line composition-root entry point. Opt-in —
             CompositionProfile.Standard with the log-and-serve default is
             byte-for-byte the prior behaviour (GP 11/13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\BootVerificationPreflight.fs" />
        <!-- The hardening baseline observed on the composed
             pipeline at boot (a probe through IServerHost.Invoke plus the
             container's reads), judged against a declared floor. AFTER
             BootVerificationPreflight (its policy names a CompositionProfile
             and its refusal is a CompositionProfileRefusal case), after
             IServerHost / ServerBinding / the preflight aggregator (it reads
             each); BEFORE ServerApp, whose run observes it between compose and
             serve. The report reads it through the tier-neutral mirror in
             DeploymentVerificationReport.fs, the way it reads the egress
             handler. Opt-in: nothing is probed unless the verification route
             is mounted or a policy is declared (GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\HostingBaseline.fs" />
        <!-- The grounding envelope sealed past boot: the enumerated
             grounding-relevant mutation surface (metric / subject registration,
             purpose declaration, canonical-method selection, disclosure policy),
             its digestible envelope projection, the single audited mutation
             choke point, and the continuity proof that boot seal + recorded
             mutation chain accounts for the live envelope. Closes the post-boot
             gap own doc names, the op-stream way rather than the
             freeze way. After BootVerificationPreflight (reads CompositionProfile
             + the seal discipline), after CompositionManifest (projects it) and
             AuditLog (emits mutations + refusals through the audit seam); before
             ServerApp. Opt-in — a deployment that composes no mutator is
             byte-for-byte unchanged (GP 11/13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\GroundingEnvelopeSeal.fs" />
        <!-- ComponentId-keyed hosted-tree usage telemetry export:
             IHostedTreeUsageExport (Record usage / Snapshot scope-isolated) +
             NoOp default + in-memory reference. Widens the fault
             signal to interaction/usage keyed by ComponentId;
             scope-isolated by construction (GP 4), zero-cost when unused
             (GP 13). Depends only on Core ComponentId; standalone. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\HostedTreeUsageExport.fs" />
        <!-- Composition well-formedness preflight: pure
             rules-as-data over the CompositionManifest (duplicate ComponentId,
             companion-slot legality, orphaned tool references) + the first-
             party IConfigValidator that runs them. After CompositionManifest
             (reads it); before ServerApp (run folds the validator into the
             extension ServiceConfig hook). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionValidator.fs" />
        <!-- Composition-inspector handler + its compose-time
             snapshot. AFTER CompositionManifest.fs / GroundingEnvelopeSeal.fs
             / CompositionValidator.fs (it projects all three) and BEFORE
             ServerApp.fs (run takes the snapshot and appends the route). That
             ordering is why this route is not mounted by BuildRouteHandlers
             like every other admin surface - see the file header. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionInspectorHandler.fs" />
        <!-- The reflection tools + the describe renderer. AFTER
             CompositionInspectorHandler.fs and DeploymentVerificationReport.fs
             (it serves both) and BEFORE ServerApp.fs (run registers the
             renderer beside the inspector snapshot). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ReflectionTools.fs" />
        <Compile Include="Server\ServerApp.fs" />
        <!-- Detachable module-binding manifest reader. After
             ServerApp (it applies stamps onto ServerModule). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ModuleBindingManifest.fs" />
        <!-- Module-binding revocation list (crypto-free format +
             parser + stampId) + file-backed transparency log. The signed
             loader lives in ToolUp.ArtefactSigning (reuses the JWS verify
             primitives). Core types only — order-independent. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ModuleBindingRevocation.fs" />
        <!-- Live-session compose surface: options + SSE
             subscribe endpoint (scope-isolated, rate-limited) +
             LiveSessionsCompose.withLiveSessions. After ServerApp (the
             record it extends via ComposeExtensions). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\Compose\LiveSessionsCompose.fs" />
        <!-- Component-scoped configuration resolution: merge a
             declared ComponentConfig section with its id-scoped env override
             + the IConfigValidator that rejects a stray override at
             preflight. After ServerApp (validators wire through the
             aggregator) + the Core ComponentConfig type. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentConfigResolver.fs" />
        <!-- Component secret & config requirements: derive a
             component's knob requirements from its config section,
             merge the residual declared secret requirements on top, and check
             PRESENCE at preflight (required secrets resolve in ISecretStore —
             existence only, never a value; required knobs bind). Two
             IConfigValidators, split on the class boundary: the knob
             check is structural-class (unbypassable), the secret probe is
             external-probe class (skippable — the store may be a remote
             vault). After ComponentConfigResolver.fs (reads the resolved
             sections) and CompositionValidator.fs (reuses its defect
             severity). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentRequirements.fs" />
        <!-- Composable-surface descriptor: forge's AVAILABLE
             composition vocabulary (companion slots + substrate reqs + config
             knob schemas + module contract), derived by reflecting the live
             ServerApp / ServerConfig registry. After ServerApp (reflects its
             record fields); complements the instance manifest. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComposableSurface.fs" />
        <!-- Module-surface descriptor: what ONE module provides
             (data types + wire TypeNames, query keys, tools, routes, jobs,
             metrics, config fields, pages) and needs (implied substrate, flag
             keys, event topics), derived from its own registrations. After
             ServerApp (reads / reflects ServerModule) and beside the
             platform-level ComposableSurface it mirrors one level down. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ModuleSurface.fs" />
        <!-- The seam-authority gate's production call site: for
             each composed module, the substrate seams its registrations imply
             are checked through the ISeamAuthorityGate, with
             refusals riding the audited observer onto the
             ledger. After ModuleSurface.fs (whose Needs projection IS the
             reach derivation, so the SDK carries one declaration-to-substrate
             map rather than two) and after BootVerificationPreflight.fs
             (whose VerifiedCompositionProfile builds the audited gate). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\SeamAuthorityEnforcement.fs" />
        <!-- Event-topology manifest: the inter-module messaging
             graph as data (per-ComponentId Emits / SubscribesTo), derived from
             live registrations — OnEvent job triggers (IEventStore
             subscriptions), AIToolDefinition.EmitsActions (notification-channel
             module actions), and an opt-in ObservingEventStore decorator that
             records emissions off ModuleEvent.SourceModule. Plus the dead-topic
             / orphan-subscription queries, an id-keyed diff for the
             golden-file gate, and the opt-in structural-class preflight
             validator. After ServerApp (reads ServerModule) and
             CompositionValidator (reuses its defect / rule-descriptor types);
             beside ModuleSurface, whose per-module lens it aggregates. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\EventTopology.fs" />
        <!-- Component data-footprint manifest: what each composed
             component stores and where, derived from the live registrations
             (registered DataTypes attributed to their producing module,
             composed audit sinks attributed to their own multi-impl id), with
             the residual companion footprint + the ContainsPii judgement
             declared on top. Plus the composition join over the
             manifest (the effect-join shape applied to data-at-rest)
             and the opt-in structural-class DSR/offboarding completeness
             preflight. After ServerApp (reads ServerModule / ServerApp
             accumulators), CompositionManifest (the join restricts to it) and
             CompositionValidator (reuses its defect / rule-descriptor types);
             beside EventTopology, the sibling derived lens. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\DataFootprint.fs" />
        <!-- Composition scale-readiness planner: the
             per-companion distributed-readiness declarations joined across a
             manifest into a per-component scale finding + a
             whole-composition verdict (the MEET of the parts), the
             vocabulary consulted for the companion swap that would lift a
             scale-limiting finding, and an opt-in structural-class preflight
             gate reading the topology intent a deployment already declares
             (ServerConfig.ReplicaCount / ServerlessHost). After
             ComposableSurface (reads its slot vocabulary), CompositionManifest
             (the join walks it) and CompositionValidator (reuses its defect /
             rule-descriptor types); beside EventTopology / DataFootprint, the
             sibling derived lenses. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ScaleReadiness.fs" />
        <!-- The operational-telemetry diode: a consent-gated
             (default off) outbound channel whose wire schema is CLOSED — no
             string field anywhere in OperationalTelemetryFrame's transitive
             closure, so it structurally cannot carry row data — plus the
             per-section consent projection, canonical rendering, and the local
             transmission journal every frame is recorded in. Standalone: no
             ServerApp, no manifest, no transport (the outbound side is the
             structural DiodeTransmit function seam, GP 1), so it sits before
             ApplianceProfile and depends on nothing above it. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\OperationalTelemetryDiode.fs" />
        <!--.A/B/D — the appliance deployment profile: the declared
             offline boot posture (external-probe-class validators downgraded to
             Warning via a decorator, so the aggregator's "any Error
             aborts" contract is untouched and the security /
             structural markers still abort), signed upgrade verification
             against provenance (both digests + the detached JWS,
             through the structural VerifyDetachedJws seam) with the pre-flip
             verify → migrate-preview → flip staging check over the
             requirements, and the data-class-aware bundle variant
             masking against the classification vocabulary. After
             ConfigValidatorAggregator (reads its classify),
             ComponentRequirements (the 432 join), CompositionManifest and
             CompositionValidator (reuses its defect / rule-descriptor types). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ApplianceProfile.fs" />
        <!-- Offline entitlement verification: the signed
             capability-token model (capability set + capacity grants + validity
             window + holder id), its canonical signed byte form, and the
             offline resolve that establishes a lifecycle phase without a
             network call in the path. Verification reuses
             structural VerifyDetachedJws seam rather than inventing a second
             shape, so it comes after ApplianceProfile; it also reads that
             file's ApplianceProfile.ClockSkewTolerance through a one-line
             bridge, which is a value read and not a dependency — entitlements
             are not appliance-only. Expiry is NOT a refusal here (that is the
             whole fail-safe posture), and EntitlementFloor's read + export
             capabilities are refused by EntitlementGovernance.declare, so no
             representable configuration withholds a customer's own data. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\EntitlementToken.fs" />
        <!--.B/C — the two places entitlement state has to reach: the
             flag ceiling that caps governed keys at what the
             entitlement grants (a decorator OVER FlagEvaluator, not an
             IFlagSource — a source is consulted only when no scope set the key,
             so one Platform-scope override would lift the entitlement
             entirely), and the structural-class boot preflight that surfaces
             days-remaining / grace / lapse loudly and NEVER returns Error,
             because a Error aborts the boot and a boot that will not
             start is the most complete way to withhold a customer's own data.
             After EntitlementToken (its types) and FlagEvaluator (the record it
             decorates). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\EntitlementValidator.fs" />
        <!-- The prover's own lifecycle: a manifest version +
             per-rule semver over every rule family that exports in the
             CompositionRuleDescriptor vocabulary, preflight-result
             stamping (what a conclusion was proven under), and the errata
             channel (published data answering "was this stamped result
             evaluated under an erratum-affected rule version?"). After
             CompositionValidator, EventTopology and DataFootprint — it seeds
             versions from all three exported manifests — and after
             ConfigValidatorAggregator (stamps a ValidatorOutcome run). Pure:
             registers nothing, decorates nothing. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionRuleVersioning.fs" />
        <!-- Authorization-surface manifest: every externally
             reachable thing a component contributes (route prefixes + exact
             route overrides under their admit sets, remoting API
             record fields through the classifier, AI-drivable tools,
             OnEvent job handlers) with its resolved default-deny
             classification — explicit requirement / inherited default-deny /
             anonymous-reachable. Plus the ActionPolicy resolution
             over the floor entries, and a severity-bearing id-keyed diff for
             the golden-file gate. After ServerApp (reads
             ServerModule) and Remoting\Auth.fs (reads the dispatcher's own
             AuthClassifier, so the manifest cannot drift from what is
             enforced); beside EventTopology / DataFootprint, the sibling
             derived lenses. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\AuthorizationSurface.fs" />
        <!-- Module-access attestation certificate: a signed,
             third-party-verifiable statement of a module's declared grant
             policy, the consent records live at an instant, and the
             grant-authority manifest hash, carried as a DSSE-wrapped in-toto
             statement over the IStatementEnvelopeSigner seam. After
             GrantPolicyGuard.fs / GrantConsentStore.fs (the 551 registry and
             the 552 resolveLive judgement it attests), DsseEnvelope.fs (the
             envelope it emits) and AuthorizationSurface.fs (the 554 surface
             it hashes). On demand only — nothing composes it. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\AccessAttestation.fs" />
        <!-- in-handler gate declarations for the platform-tier
             API records (JobApi / ModelExecutionApi / IModuleQueryBusApi).
             After AuthorizationSurface.fs, which declares the record they
             are expressed in. IFormApi's live in ToolUp.Forms.Server,
             beside its own handler. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\PlatformInHandlerGates.fs" />
        <!-- Component provenance: which package/assembly+version
             a composed companion came from, keyed by the same ComponentId the
             manifest carries (id-join, no manifest-shape change). After
             ServerApp (walks the composed companion set). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentProvenance.fs" />
        <!-- Host-envelope descriptor: what THIS deployment offers
             a module — composed capability layers, every companion slot marked
             filled or open, each composed module's ModuleSurface, the
             config-knob schemas with the values this deployment resolved, the
             occupied route prefixes, and the platform build — plus canonical
             JSON + a SHA-256 stamp so an external authoring tool pins a
             snapshot and detects staleness. After ServerApp / CompositionManifest
             (the composed instance it projects), ComposableSurface.fs (the slot
             + knob universe it joins against), ModuleSurface.fs (the per-module
             surfaces it aggregates) and ComponentProvenance.fs (the platform
             version). Pure — registers nothing, decorates nothing (GP 11/13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\HostEnvelope.fs" />
        <!-- Component health rollup: IHealthCheck results keyed by
             ComponentId into a per-component rollup (+ an Unkeyed bucket).
             After ServerApp (reads app.HealthChecks). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentHealthRollup.fs" />
        <!-- Component lifecycle ordering: a declarative
             init-before partial order over ComponentIds + a stable
             topological init/dispose driver (dispose = reverse); a cycle is
             rejected at compose. Standalone (ComponentId only). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentLifecycle.fs" />
        <!-- Live composition hot-swap: swap a declared companion
             impl on a running app by ComponentId, driven by the
             lifecycle order (init new, atomic re-point, dispose old), atomic
             with rollback. Opt-in (HotSwapMode, default off). After
             ComponentLifecycle. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionHotSwap.fs" />
        <!-- Declarative composition descriptor: the serializable
             inverse of the manifest (component selection by
             ComponentId + ServerConfig) + RegistrationCatalogue +
             CompositionDescriptor.ofManifest / ServerApp.ofManifest. After
             ServerApp (folds addModule / with* builders). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDescriptor.fs" />
        <!-- Descriptor schema-version + forward migration: an
             older CompositionDescriptor migrates to the current shape before
             ServerApp.ofManifest composes it; a too-new version fails
             readably. Hosts the versioned ServerApp.ofManifest (runs migrate
             first). After CompositionDescriptor.fs. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs" />
        <!-- Per-tenant composition presets: resolve a tenant to a
             base preset descriptor + per-tenant hole bindings + per-tenant
             component config, composed via ofManifest;
             scope-isolated by construction. After CompositionDescriptor.fs
             (holes/apply) + ComponentConfigResolver.fs. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\TenantCompositionPreset.fs" />
        <!-- Null-composition dry-run harness: rebind every
             companion slot to the in-process default the slot already
             declares (derived from the reflected slot set — leaving
             a slot None IS selecting its default), rebuild through the
             versioned ofManifest, run the
             structural-class well-formedness rules, drive the
             init/dispose order, and return a typed DryRunReport — zero
             external services, defects as findings rather than exceptions.
             Plus the Expecto-shaped (Expecto-free) DryRun.shouldCompose
             affordance for consumer suites + worked-example verification.
             After
             CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs (the versioned build path it
             drives), ComposableSurface.fs (the slot universe it null-binds),
             ComponentLifecycle.fs and CompositionValidator.fs. Nothing
             registers into DI — a consumer that never calls it composes
             byte-for-byte what it did before (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDryRun.fs" />
        <!-- Cross-version composition upgrade planner: given this
             instance's manifest + provenance and the
             ComposableSurface of a NEWER version set (data, so no new
             binaries need loading), compute a typed CompositionUpgradePlan —
             which composed slots' contracts widened / changed / vanished, which
             descriptor schema hops the jump crosses in what order,
             and the convention-derived docs/migrations/<slug>.md pointer per
             step. structural diff applied across versions rather
             than across instances: both sides' slots are projected into the
             ComponentEntry shape (contract fingerprinted into Impl) so
             CompositionDiff.diff does the id-keyed pairing. After
             CompositionDiff.fs, ComposableSurface.fs, ComponentProvenance.fs,
             CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs (its migration-error rendering) and
             CompositionDryRun.fs (its slotInterface parser). Pure — nothing
             registers into DI, nothing runs at compose (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionUpgradePlan.fs" />
        <!-- The cumulative privacy-budget ledger, MOVED here
             from the federation companion (it was
             InterPlatform/Server/PrivacyBudgetLedger.fs,). Two
             tiers now meter against it — the clean-room gate and the
             grounding tier's declassification routines — and a second
             implementation of a privacy control is how a path that
             enforces slightly less appears, so the seam sits at the layer
             both already depend on rather than minting a companion ->
             companion package edge (GP 1). Appended last: it needs
             IConditionalBlobStorage (Core) and the FableConverters set
             (Server/Remoting/Json/), and nothing above it needs it. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\PrivacyBudgetLedger.fs" />
        <!-- The scope-enumeration seam (IScopeEnumerator + its
             ITeamStore-backed default) and the converged restart-recovery
             sweep (IIngestionRecoverySurface + IngestionRecoverySweep) the
             RAG and KnowledgeBase companions now share. After
             Teams\TeamManagement.fs (the default adapts ITeamStore.ListTeams
             rather than adding a member to it) and IngestionStatusStore.fs
             (the RAG-side surface adapter wraps IIngestionStatusStore).
             Nothing here registers into DI and nothing runs at compose — a
             deployment that composes no enumerator and no sweep is
             byte-for-byte unchanged (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ScopeEnumeration.fs" />
        <!-- The N-party countersignature registry: a signed
             propose / review / approve / revoke lifecycle over arbitrary
             content-hashed subjects, with approval live only under every
             enrolled party's signature over the exact subject hash. Placed
             last because it depends only on things far above it — the Core
             signed-shape separators, IBlobStorage, IdentitySanitiser and the
             shared JSON converter set — and nothing in the file is composed
             by default, so nothing below needs to see it (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CountersignatureRegistry.fs" />
    </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Giraffe" />
    <!-- 0.4.4 — ToolUp.Remoting.{Json,Server,Giraffe,AspNetCore}
         PackageReferences dropped; source folded under Server/Remoting/
         per the Compile block above. Microsoft.IO.RecyclableMemoryStream
         was a transitive dep of ToolUp.Remoting.Server / Giraffe /
         AspNetCore — now declared explicitly. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IO.RecyclableMemoryStream" />
    <!-- The self-hosted log store's default backend. MIT,
         freely available, no paid tier (GP 2); the version is pinned
         centrally in Directory.Packages.props. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite" />
    <!-- Ed25519 signing / verification for
         IArtifactSigner / IArtifactVerifier defaults. MIT-licensed
         (GP 2 — no paid deps). Version pinned centrally in
         Directory.Packages.props. -->
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" />
    <!-- 0.4.4 — explicit FSharp.Core PackageReference. Pre-fold, the
         transitively-resolved FSharp.Core was 10.1.300 (Directory.Packages.props
         pins). Post-fold, one of the dropped ToolUp.Remoting.* packages
         no longer floors FSharp.Core, and NuGet picks 6.0.0 from a
         lower dep — which lacks the `objnull` type the F# 10 compiler
         emits. Explicit reference forces the centrally-pinned version
         back into scope. -->
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
